# Third-party pins shared across the Chiron images built in this repository.
#
# Sourced by scripts/publish_docker_image.sh and passed to each build as
# --build-arg. The Dockerfiles declare the matching ARG with no default and fail
# loudly if it is missing, so a pin can never be silently picked up from a
# Dockerfile that was left behind during a bump.
#
# The image VERSION is not here. It is `version` in worker/pyproject.toml, which
# is also the version of the chiron-platform package installed into the base, so
# there is one number rather than two that can disagree. The tabula repository
# carries the same number for chiron-tabula. See README.md.
#
# BIOENGINE_REF and HYPHA_RPC_PIN are duplicated in the tabula repository's
# docker/versions.env, because chiron-tabula installs bioengine itself. Bump them
# together.
#
# BIOENGINE_REF is the one to edit most often. It is consumed by the LAST layer
# of every model image, so changing it here and rebuilding reuses every cached
# layer up to that point (torch, flash-attn, the model stack) and reinstalls
# only bioengine itself.

# bioengine commit to install. f8e65bc = v0.16.1, the tip of main on
# 2026-08-28. Five minor versions on from the previous pin, taken as one step
# because bioengine publishes no releases and every intermediate commit is
# equally untagged.
#
# What the jump changes for us:
#  - The proxy's health check no longer calls check_health on the entry
#    deployment. It reads each sibling deployment's RUNNING replica count out
#    of the Serve controller instead, so a saturated app neither blocks nor
#    fails the probe. That is issue #152, and it is exactly the remove_when of
#    the chiron patch bioengine-proxy-entry-health-tolerance, which is dropped
#    here.
#  - App source is no longer shipped to Ray as a py_module. Apps are imported
#    through the bootstrap finder installed by bioengine/__init__.py.
#  - format_version 0.6.0 and the manifests are unchanged, but @bioengine.app
#    is not: it now rejects num_gpus and sizes GPUs by VRAM through
#    gpu_memory_mb. The manager and the orchestrator drop the argument (an
#    omitted VRAM request is a CPU-only app) and CHIRON_TRAINER_DEPLOYMENT
#    declares gpu_memory_mb=-1, bioengine's portable whole GPU, which is what
#    num_gpus=1 reserved before.
#
# Still open upstream, so the patches that work around them stay: bioengine
# #164 pinned service lookup 404s, bioengine #165 a busy app read as a dead
# replica, bioengine #166 runtime_env pins app venvs to the declared floor.
#
# Prior pin 4e73d9d was 0.11.19 + PR #136 (authenticated ICE fetch, TURN
# credential rotation, abandoned-peer sweep), which is what made pure-WebRTC
# weight transfer hold. Prior pin f9d04cf was 0.11.18 + PR #135. Prior pin
# 815234f was 0.11.17 + PR #134.
BIOENGINE_REF=f8e65bc

# hypha_rpc floor. bioengine pulls hypha_rpc in transitively and accepts a wide
# range, so without a floor here a rebuild picks up whatever the resolver
# happens to land on and a WebRTC fix can silently disappear from an image.
#
# 0.21.47 is the release that carries oeway/hypha-rpc#166: a data channel is now
# addressed with the workspace the ANSWERING peer reports rather than the
# caller's own. Chiron needs that on every WebRTC run, because the orchestrator
# connects with the operator's token and therefore lives in 'ws-user-<id>' while
# the trainers live in the worker's workspace. Below this version the first call
# over the channel is addressed to a workspace the trainer is not in and hangs
# with no error. Chiron carried its own patch for this from 0.7.6; the patch is
# dropped at this pin because upstream now does the same thing.
# Quoted, because an unquoted ">" in a sourced file is a shell redirection:
# bash reads HYPHA_RPC_PIN=hypha_rpc and then creates a file called "=0.21.47".
HYPHA_RPC_PIN="hypha_rpc>=0.21.47"

# scGPT commit to install. Pinned to a SHA rather than tracking main because
# everything we need from scGPT is unreleased: main added
# scgpt/tokenizer/vocab_compat.py with a pure-Python BuiltinVocab fallback, which
# is what removes the dependency on the archived torchtext, and this particular
# commit is PR #351 "cuda-12.8 and FlashAttention 2.x compatibility", which adds
# the flash_attn_compat.py shim that lets scGPT drive the same
# flash_attn.modules.mha.MHA class Tabula uses. PyPI scgpt 0.2.4 predates both
# and is unusable: it hard-depends on torchtext, which is archived and has no
# wheels for modern Python or torch.
SCGPT_REF=cebd6fae655b9c585a4807daa3ac31bb764f06b4
